dozens dead and dozens injured after a  fire caused a stampede among worshipers  at a coptic christian church in the  egyptian city of giza  the incident happened as thousands  gathered for morning mass at the abu  safin church  i saw people jumping from the upper  floor suffocation suffocation all of  them did so many dead and there are  children we didn't know how to get to  them we didn't know whose son this is or  whose daughter that is how is this  possible  giza sits at the southern edge of the  greater cairo area one of the most  densely populated places in the world  dilapidated infrastructure means  accidental fires are common  made more likely due to the record high  temperatures across the region  the fire in abu safin church thought to  have been caused by a faulty air  conditioner  we started to see from the outside that  the smoke was getting bigger and people  were wanting to jump from the upper  floor of the building of the church to  the next and one did then we went inside  and found the children and we started to  take the bodies out  in the aftermath of the incident  president abdel fattah al-sisi announced  the mobilization of quote all state  services to ensure that all measures are  taken the prosecutor's office has also  opened an investigation  some of the injured were firefighters  the blaze blocked an exit trapping  churchgoers and causing the stampede  according to eyewitnesses most of those  killed were children  zane basravi al-jazeera  let's bring in adam  for an update he's a journalist based in  cairo welcome to al jazeera so the  official death toll right now stands at  41 can we expect it to be much higher  it is expected to start to be a little  bit higher not much as far as the  official figures from the government is  concerned the health ministry confirmed  that as you've said 41 have been  died in the fire and 14  are injured this is the number that the  health ministry has registered and is  giving health care services too among  these 14 for are in critical conditions  they are in intensive care units where  health officials are treating them and  trying to make their health condition  steady as much as possible from the 10  remaining two have been  given the green light to go home they've  been dismissed from the hospital and  they are in good condition to go home  the rest are being treated but according  to the health ministry most of their  injuries  injuries are not so concerning so it  might  increase a little bit due to the four  and the uh remaining critical condition  and remain to be in the icu units  tell us a little bit more about the  church itself and the area that the  church is located in because presumably  it would be a highly congested area in  in giza  definitely it is a district called  imbaba one of the most  populous and dense population dense  districts in  greater cairo it is known to have a  general average socioeconomic background  this is a sunday service and of course  it means that the church is usually at  its full capacity it's at his busiest um  prayer service all over the week and  therefore the numbers of people there is  quite um significant it is the biggest  number ever all over the week uh finally  the church itself because of the  district um and its dynasty the church  is not a common structure church it's  not a big facility with a huge area of  land and many  entries and exit points it's more or  less like a  residential building um in terms of its  design and therefore the exits and  entries to that building are not so many  and because according to the health  ministry the fire that was sparked by  one of the ac  air conditioning devices in the second  floor um there was huge smoke and most  people could not get out and many of  them died because of suffocation from  the smoke rather rather from the flames  itself this is what we know so far in  terms of the incidents and how it  unfolded  i mean this is not the first tragedy in  egypt where